.TH HD-BATTERY 1 "November 2026" "hd-laptop" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-battery \- show the battery level in a notification
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-battery
.RB [ \-\-monitor ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-battery
shows the level of the battery in a notification of mako, with whether the
charger is plugged in and the battery charges, and the time left until it is
empty or full.
The key binding
.B SUPER + SHIFT + B
of the config of Hyprland of
.BR hd-desktop (7)
runs it; on a system without
.BR hd-laptop (7)
the key does nothing.
.PP
It reads the batteries and the chargers in
.IR /sys/class/power_supply .
Batteries of devices, such as a mouse, do not count; two batteries in a
laptop count as one.
The time left comes from the power that the batteries give, as the firmware
tells it, so it changes with the load.
A battery that does not tell its power gives only its level.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-monitor
Watch the battery until stopped, and show a notification:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
when the battery falls to 50%, 25%, 10% and 5% on battery power, with the
time left until it is empty;
.IP \(bu 2
when the charger is pulled out, with the level and the time left until the
battery is empty;
.IP \(bu 2
when the charger is plugged in, with the level and the time until the battery
is full, or that it is full or not charging;
.IP \(bu 2
at the start, when the laptop runs on battery power at 50% or less.
.RE
.IP
Each warning is shown once until the charger is plugged in again; the
warnings of the levels that the battery is already at or below when the
charger is pulled out are not shown, as that notification gives the level.
Each notification takes the place of the one before it.
The batteries are read when the kernel sends an event of a power supply and
every 30 seconds.
The user unit
.B hd-battery-monitor.service
runs
.B hd-battery \-\-monitor
in the desktop session.
.PP
The notifications on battery power at 10% and below are critical and have
the warning icon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-laptop (7),
.BR mako (1),
.BR notify-send (1)
